// Adversarial stress: IronCurtain protocol with Aegis lives system — Dense layout.
//
// IronCurtain fires a distance-falloff damage wave when a bolt is lost, dealing
// damage to all cells proportional to (1 - distance / max_range). Dense layout
// packs cells tightly, maximising how many cells fall within the wave radius and
// how many cells are near the bolt-loss point (lower-wall region). This stress
// scenario targets:
//
//   1. Distance-falloff NaN on zero-distance: if the bolt is lost at a position
//      exactly coincident with a cell centre, the distance is 0.0 and the
//      falloff formula (1 - 0 / max_range) = 1.0 — safe. However, if max_range
//      is 0.0 (misconfigured or corrupted resource), the division is 0/0 = NaN.
//      NoNaN catches NaN propagation into BumpDealt message values.
//
//   2. Invulnerable-cell filter bypass: cells with Shield or similar invulnerability
//      markers must be excluded from the damage wave. Dense layout has high cell
//      density; if the filter is applied per-entity but the query accidentally
//      includes already-dead cells (Dead marker not yet processed this frame),
//      the wave applies damage to cells being destroyed concurrently, producing
//      a double-despawn that triggers a Bevy panic. NoEntityLeaks catches
//      lingering damage-wave message entities if the pipeline doesn't drain.
//
//   3. Repeated bolt-loss pressure: Aegis lives system allows multiple bolt-loss
//      events per run. With chaos action_prob 0.6, the bolt frequently falls past
//      the breaker, triggering repeated IronCurtain waves. If the wave system
//      allocates per-wave state that is not cleaned up between waves, entity
//      counts grow monotonically. NoEntityLeaks catches accumulation; BoltInBounds
//      verifies bolt respawn positions after each loss event.
//
//   4. RunStatsMonotonic coverage: each IronCurtain wave that destroys cells
//      should increment CellsDestroyed exactly once per cell. Dense layout
//      maximises simultaneous destructions. RunStatsMonotonic is not listed as
//      disallowed to keep the scenario focused, but NoNaN would catch any counter
//      wrap that becomes NaN in a downstream calculation.
//
// 3000 frames with allow_early_end: false ensures multiple bolt-loss cycles.
// 16 runs explore diverse Dense cell arrangements and bolt-loss positions.
(
    breaker: "Aegis",
    layout: "Dense",
    input: Chaos((action_prob: 0.6)),
    max_frames: 3000,
    disallowed_failures: [
        NoNaN,
        BoltInBounds,
        BreakerInBounds,
        BoltSpeedAccurate,
        ValidDashState,
        BreakerCountReasonable,
        NoEntityLeaks,
        BoltCountReasonable,
    ],
    allowed_failures: None,
    debug_setup: None,
    allow_early_end: false,
    stress: (runs: 16, parallelism: 16),
    seed: 6173,
    frame_mutations: [
        (frame: 10, mutation: InjectProtocol(kind_name: "IronCurtain")),
    ],
)
